---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout
  title="Hobbies"
  category="About | Beyond Engineering"
  year=""
  description="Personal interests of Florian Froment | design, technology, mobility and exploration."
>

  <p slot="intro" class="hero-intro">
    Beyond engineering, I am driven by curiosity, design,
    technology and the exploration of how things move,
    evolve and interact.
  </p>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      01 | Automotive
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Automotive design and engineering.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I have a strong interest in automotive engineering,
        particularly vehicle architecture, mechanical design,
        performance and the evolution of hybrid technologies.
      </p>

      <p>
        I also enjoy studying how manufacturers combine
        technical constraints, industrial design and brand identity
        to create distinctive products.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      02 | Design
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Industrial design and visual identity.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I am interested in the relationship between function
        and aesthetics | from mechanical products and machines
        to architecture, materials and graphic design.
      </p>

      <p>
        I particularly appreciate minimalist and functional
        approaches inspired by Swiss Design, industrial materials
        and contemporary product design.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      03 | Technology
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Emerging technologies and experimentation.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I enjoy exploring technologies beyond my core engineering
        work | 3D scanning, augmented reality, digital twins,
        immersive visualisation and new human-machine interfaces.
      </p>

      <p>
        Many of these explorations eventually become prototypes,
        concepts or ideas that I integrate into my engineering projects.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      04 | Travel
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Discovering new environments.
      </h2>

      <p>
        Travelling gives me the opportunity to discover different
        cultures, industrial environments and ways of approaching
        engineering and design.
      </p>

      <p>
        International experiences have also helped me become more
        adaptable and comfortable working in multicultural environments.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>


  <div class="detail-section">

    <p class="detail-index">
      05 | Making
    </p>

    <div class="detail-copy">

      <h2>
        Building things for the pleasure of understanding them.
      </h2>

      <p>
        I regularly develop personal mechanical concepts,
        prototypes and objects simply to explore an idea,
        test a mechanism or learn a new manufacturing process.
      </p>

      <p>
        For me, engineering does not stop when the professional
        project ends | experimentation is also a personal hobby.
      </p>

    </div>

  </div>

</ProjectLayout>